Modules on disk that the go.work leaves out. Shaped after kubernetes, whose
hack/update-go-workspace.sh generates go.work from `git ls-files '**/go.mod'` but adds only the
root and staging/src/k8s.io/*: at e2b96b2 that is 31 of the 34 modules on disk. The three it drops
are hack/tools, code-generator/examples, and kms/internal/plugins/_mock — build tooling, examples,
and a mock. etcd copied the same script and dropped the filter, so its go.work lists all 13
modules, then subtracts the tools again downstream for the bill of materials.

So the omission is deliberate in both, and in both it means the same thing: not the product.

Which makes it a real choice, not arithmetic. Measuring the workspace gives 100.00% here;
measuring the tree gives 42.86%, and the four uncovered statements are a code generator. Note
also that go tool cover -func cannot read the wider profile at all — the omitted module is not
required by the root, so it fails with "no required module provides package".

_mock is dropped by the walk anyway, for a reason that has nothing to do with go.work: the go
tool ignores underscore-prefixed directories, so it is not in the build to begin with.

modules_on_disk: 3
go_list_m: 2
go_list_dotdotdot: 1
discovered_modules: 3
discovered_packages: 3
packages_with_tests: 2
has_workspace: 1
modules_in_workspace: 2
modules_with_errors: 0
-- go.work --
go 1.27

use (
	.
	./staging/src/k8s.io/api
)
-- go.mod --
module k8s.test/kubernetes

go 1.27
-- root.go --
package kubernetes

func Serve() int { return 1 }
-- root_test.go --
package kubernetes

import "testing"

func TestServe(t *testing.T) {
	if Serve() != 1 {
		t.Fatal("no")
	}
}
-- staging/src/k8s.io/api/go.mod --
module k8s.test/api

go 1.27
-- staging/src/k8s.io/api/api.go --
package api

func Version() string { return "v1" }
-- staging/src/k8s.io/api/api_test.go --
package api

import "testing"

func TestVersion(t *testing.T) {
	if Version() != "v1" {
		t.Fatal("no")
	}
}
-- hack/tools/go.mod --
module k8s.test/hack/tools

go 1.27
-- hack/tools/tools.go --
package tools

func Generate() int { return 1 }
func Format() int   { return 2 }
func Lint() int     { return 3 }
func Vet() int      { return 4 }
-- staging/src/k8s.io/kms/internal/plugins/_mock/go.mod --
module k8s.test/kms/plugins/mock

go 1.27
-- staging/src/k8s.io/kms/internal/plugins/_mock/mock.go --
package mock

func Mock() int { return 0 }
